# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token.
# Get from: https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/analytics/web/sites
#   1. Add site → host: altorank.co
#   2. Disable auto-install (we ship the beacon ourselves via Base.astro)
#   3. Copy the "JS snippet token" value here
#
# Set on Cloudflare Pages: Project → Settings → Environment variables
# → both Production and Preview environments. Redeploy to activate.
PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# ── Open-source, cookieless event analytics ───────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Web Analytics above gives pageviews only. It cannot record events,
# so it cannot answer "did organic traffic reach the signup", which is an
# outbound click to app.altorank.co. Set ONE of the two providers below.
#
# Neither sets cookies nor collects personal data, so no consent banner is
# required under GDPR. Self-host either to keep the data in the EU.
#
# Umami (MIT, lighter to self-host: Postgres only)
#   Cloud free tier: https://cloud.umami.is  ·  Self-host: https://umami.is/docs
PUBLIC_UMAMI_SRC=
PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=

# Plausible (AGPL-3.0, same licence as AltoRank, EU-based; self-host needs
# Postgres + ClickHouse). Set these INSTEAD of the Umami pair, not alongside.
#   https://plausible.io/docs/self-hosting
PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_SRC=
PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=
